  "statement": "H5/H3 = \u0394\u00b2 (c5/c3) = \u0394\u00b2 (14+\u03c1)(18+\u03c1)/(16+\u03c1)\u00b2 exactly, with \u03c1 = (\u03c0/e)\u00b2 \u03bb_min(L2) = E2 = 1.0228725137857889e-02. Therefore \u221a(H5/H3) = \u0394 \u00d7 0.9921667999068299, not \u0394. The relative difference 0.78332001% equals 1 minus that structural factor (and equals 1 \u2212 3\u221a7/8 at \u03c1 = 0, which is already within 0.001% of the physical value). The identity \u221a(H5/H3) = \u0394 holds if and only if c3 = c5, i.e. in the limit \u03c1 \u2192 \u221e (clock dominates 18 and 16). It is not an identity at the archived \u03c1, and the 0.78% is not an independent coincidence."
